      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it, but 50 mg of amlodipine daily is well beyond the 10 mg maximum. I don't know of any indication that would justify it for a 70 kg adult. The risk is severe hypotension and shock, and entering the order could lead to the patient receiving that dose.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily**, or 5 mg if you'd like to titrate up. I can do either now.\n- **Add a second agent** if 10 mg isn't controlling the blood pressure. I can enter that order, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide.\n- **Call pharmacy or your attending** if there's a specific reason for this dose that I'm missing. If they approve it, it can be entered through whatever pathway your hospital requires for exceptions to dosing limits.\n\nIf I've misread something, for example if the order was meant for a different drug or a different unit, tell me and I'll correct it."
      }
     ],
